# Headed receipt of the update chip's ACTION (2026-07-24 auto-update plan, H3).
#
# The chip is the button when there is something to carry on with. Point the
# app at a feed offering a newer version, confirm the chip says so and offers
# the download, then click it and confirm the app actually starts fetching —
# a click that changes nothing would look identical in a still capture.
#
#   HOCKET_UPDATE_FEED=<feed> HOCKET_UPDATE_PUBKEY=<key> \
#   HOCKET_SCENARIO=scenarios/update_action.scn HOCKET_CAPTURE_DIR=<dir> \
#     <installed hocket>
#
# Must run the INSTALLED build; a dev binary reports itself un-updatable and
# the chip stays a plain label.
settle 40
assert text Version
assert text download
capture 01_update_actionable
click .update-action download
# Frames, not seconds: a 34MB fetch plus BLAKE3 and signature verification
# needs far more than the ~0.4s that `settle 25` buys at 60fps.
settle 400
# Proof the click did work rather than merely being clickable: only a
# completed, verified download reaches "ready, restart to finish". The bytes
# are held in memory by the transport, so nothing is left staged on disk
# when this process exits.
assert text restart
capture 02_after_click
log update chip action captured
